{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>The hidden things belong to YHWH our Elohim.</b> And if you say: What is in our power to do? You punish the many for the thoughts of the individual, as it is said ״פֶּן יֵשׁ בָּכֶם אִישׁ״ and so on, and afterwards ״וְרָאוּ אֶת מַכּוֹת הָאָרֶץ הַהִוא״ — but surely a person does not know his fellow's hidden thoughts! [He replies:] I do not punish you for the hidden things — they belong to YHWH our Elohim, and He will exact payment from that individual. But ״the revealed things belong to us and to our children״ — to eradicate the evil from our midst, and if we do not execute justice upon them, the many will be punished. It is pointed (with dots) over <b>לנו ולבנינו</b> to expound that even for the revealed things He did not punish the many until they crossed the Jordan — from when they accepted upon themselves the oath at Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal and became guarantors for one another (Sotot 37; see Sanhedrin 43)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:55.888746954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}